# The repository-wide .gitignore excludes any directory named `gen` (line 397),
# which is why `ffi/.gitignore` re-includes `poc/*/gen/**`. This slice's
# generator sits one level deeper (`poc/python/mech/gen/`), where that
# re-inclusion does not reach, so it is re-included here instead. Checked with
# `git check-ignore`, which is the rule `ffi/.gitignore` states after the same
# word cost three sessions.
#
# It matters more than it looks: README R4's last paragraph is that a figure
# whose harness is not in the tree cannot be defended at all, and the Rust
# slice's withdrawn encode column is what that cost. `gen/out/**` is emitted
# source and every measured artifact is compiled from it, so it is committed.
!mech/gen/
!mech/gen/**

# Build output, and only build output.
mech/build/
mech/pyo3/target/
__pycache__/
